namespace trion:
    use formal

    section "Nouns and verbs":
        A noun denotes an entity.
        A verb denotes a relation among entities.
        Each term has exactly one meaning.

        [WORD-NO-OUTSIDE-KNOWLEDGE]
        The trion processor shall derive the meaning of each term from the statements of the specification.

        example DESCRIBED-TERMS:
            kind consistency
            input """
Each room has exactly one owner.
[A] The owner of a room may archive the room.
"""
            expect consistent

    section "Names and target constraints":
        Each canonical symbol has exactly one owning namespace.
        Each alias denotes a canonical symbol.
        Each canonical symbol has a symbol kind.
        Each specification reference names a specification.
        Each specification application has a target mapping.
        Each derived class has a nominal formula.
        Each target description states a target constraint.

        [WORD-RESOLVE-ALIAS]
        The trion processor shall resolve each alias to the canonical symbol of the alias.

        [WORD-CHECK-KIND]
        The trion processor shall check each symbol kind.

        [WORD-REFERENCE]
        The trion processor shall resolve each specification reference.

        [WORD-APPLY-SPECIFICATION]
        The trion processor shall apply each contract of a specification application to the corresponding target.

        [WORD-CHECK-FORM-BINDING]
        The trion processor shall check each form binding against the statements of the target of the form binding.

        [WORD-EXPAND-CLASS]
        The trion processor shall expand each derived class into the nominal formula of the derived class.

        [WORD-TARGET-CONSTRAINT]
        The trion processor shall read each target description as a target constraint.
